{"availability":"available","full":"olivierluethy/IntelliGrade","name":"IntelliGrade","description":"An efficient app which can be used for school grades. #javascript","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2023-01-25T20:34:26Z","updated":"2026-10-05T00:55:21Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://olivierluethy.github.io/IntelliGrade/","topics":["grade-calculator","gradebook","gradepro"],"demo":"https://olivierluethy.github.io/IntelliGrade/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T00:55:29.614Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T00:55:29.614Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T00:55:29.614Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T02:37:14.169Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T09:05:03.523Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T00:55:29.614Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A grade-tracking and academic-planning app for students.","“What grade do I need on my next exam?” — answered in one glance.","IntelliGrade is a client-side web app that helps a student track their grades and plan toward a target. You enter your grades (or the points you scored), set the average you're aiming for, and the app tells you — in plain language — exactly what you need on your remaining exams to get there."],"features":["You need 5.25 on each of your 2 upcoming exams to reach your target of 5.00.","It also shows your current gap and how much you can still afford to slip. The exam count is prefilled from the subject's scheduled exams, so it stays in sync automatically."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/olivierluethy/IntelliGrade/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4600775bbc5f8b9b442cc521b774694eb6dc05e243e500921475f4917b5664a7","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:14.321Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T02:37:14.321Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A grade-tracking and academic-planning app for students.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/